{"id":"mahabharata-3-201","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":201,"title":"एकाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 201 · The senses and their control","summary":{"en":"The hunter explains how the mind runs after the objects of the senses, how desire and anger arise from them, and how the wise man sees these faults beforehand and masters the senses. He describes the twenty-four principles of the manifest and unmanifest.","kn":"ಮನಸ್ಸು ಇಂದ್ರಿಯವಿಷಯಗಳ ಹಿಂದೆ ಓಡುವುದನ್ನು, ಅವುಗಳಿಂದ ಕಾಮಕ್ರೋಧಗಳು ಹುಟ್ಟುವುದನ್ನು, ಜ್ಞಾನಿ ಈ ದೋಷಗಳನ್ನು ಮೊದಲೇ ಕಂಡು ಇಂದ್ರಿಯಗಳನ್ನು ಗೆಲ್ಲುವುದನ್ನು ವ್ಯಾಧನು ವಿವರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವ್ಯಕ್ತಾವ್ಯಕ್ತದ ಇಪ್ಪತ್ತನಾಲ್ಕು ತತ್ತ್ವಗಳನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"व्याध समझाता है कि मन इन्द्रियों के विषयों के पीछे कैसे दौड़ता है, उनसे काम और क्रोध कैसे उठते हैं, और ज्ञानी इन दोषों को पहले ही देखकर इन्द्रियों को वश में करता है। वह व्यक्त और अव्यक्त के चौबीस तत्त्वों का वर्णन करता है।","te":"మనస్సు ఇంద్రియ విషయాల వెంట ఎలా పరుగెడుతుందో, వాటి నుండి కామక్రోధాలు ఎలా పుడతాయో, జ్ఞాని ఈ దోషాలను ముందే చూసి ఇంద్రియాలను ఎలా జయిస్తాడో వ్యాధుడు వివరిస్తాడు. వ్యక్తావ్యక్తాల ఇరవై నాలుగు తత్త్వాలను వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"மனம் புலன் பொருள்களின் பின் ஓடுவதையும், அவற்றிலிருந்து ஆசையும் சினமும் எழுவதையும், ஞானி இக்குறைகளை முன்பே கண்டு புலன்களை வெல்வதையும் வ்யாதன் விளக்குகிறான். வ்யக்த, அவ்யக்தத்தின் இருபத்து நான்கு தத்துவங்களை விவரிக்கிறான்.","ml":"ഇന്ദ്രിയവിഷയങ്ങൾക്കുപിന്നാലെ മനസ്സ് ഓടുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും, അവയിൽനിന്ന് കാമവും ക്രോധവും ഉണ്ടാകുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും വ്യാധൻ വിശദീകരിക്കുന്നു; ജ്ഞാനി ഈ ദോഷങ്ങൾ മുൻകൂട്ടി കണ്ട് ഇന്ദ്രിയങ്ങളെ നിയന്ത്രിക്കുന്നു. വ്യക്തവും അവ്യക്തവുമായ ഇരുപത്തിനാലു തത്ത്വങ്ങളെയും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.201; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु विप्रेण धर्मव्याधो युधिष्ठिर ।\nप्रत्युवाच यथा विप्रं तच्छृणुष्व नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed thus by the brahmin, Yudhishthira, the dharma-hunter answered him; listen to how, lord of men."}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"विज्ञानार्थं मनुष्याणां मनः पूर्वं प्रवर्तते ।\nतत्प्राप्य कामं भजते क्रोधं च द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the sake of knowing things, the mind of men goes out first; reaching an object it takes up desire and anger, best of brahmins."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततस्तदर्थं यतते कर्म चारभते महत् ।\nइष्टानां रूपगन्धानामभ्यासं च निषेवते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he strives for that object, begins great undertakings, and gives himself repeatedly to the pleasing forms and scents."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो रागः प्रभवति द्वेषश्च तदनन्तरम् ।\nततो लोभः प्रभवति मोहश्च तदनन्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From that arises attachment, and after that aversion; from that greed arises, and after that delusion."}},{"n":5,"text":"तस्य लोभाभिभूतस्य रागद्वेषहतस्य च ।\nन धर्मे जायते बुद्धिर्व्याजाद्धर्मं करोति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one overcome by greed and struck by attachment and aversion, understanding does not arise in dharma, and he practises dharma only as a pretext."}},{"n":6,"text":"व्याजेन चरते धर्ममर्थं व्याजेन रोचते ।\nव्याजेन सिध्यमानेषु धनेषु द्विजसत्तम ।\nतत्रैव रमते बुद्धिस्ततः पापं चिकीर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He follows dharma by pretext, and likes wealth by pretext; and in wealth that is gained by pretext, best of brahmins, his mind delights, and then he wishes to do sin."}},{"n":7,"text":"सुहृद्भिर्वार्यमाणश्च पण्डितैश्च द्विजोत्तम ।\nउत्तरं श्रुतिसंबद्धं ब्रवीति श्रुतियोजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When friends and wise men restrain him, he replies with an answer tied to scripture, as if applying scripture."}},{"n":8,"text":"अधर्मस्त्रिविधस्तस्य वर्धते रागदोषतः ।\nपापं चिन्तयते चापि ब्रवीति च करोति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"For him, from the fault of attachment, threefold unrighteousness grows: he thinks sin, speaks it and does it."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्याधर्मप्रवृत्तस्य गुणा नश्यन्ति साधवः ।\nएकशीलाश्च मित्रत्वं भजन्ते पापकर्मिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For him engaged in unrighteousness the good qualities perish, and sinners of the same character become his friends."}},{"n":10,"text":"स तेनासुखमाप्नोति परत्र च विहन्यते ।\nपापात्मा भवति ह्येवं धर्मलाभं तु मे शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because of that he gets unhappiness and is struck down in the next world. Thus a sinful person comes to be; now hear from me how dharma is gained."}},{"n":11,"text":"यस्त्वेतान्प्रज्ञया दोषान्पूर्वमेवानुपश्यति ।\nकुशलः सुखदुःखेषु साधूंश्चाप्युपसेवते ।\nतस्य साधुसमारम्भाद्बुद्धिर्धर्मेषु जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The one who sees these faults beforehand by wisdom, who is skilled in pleasure and pain, and who also serves good people, in him, through the company of the good, understanding in dharma arises."}},{"text":"ब्राह्मण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The brahmin said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"ब्रवीषि सूनृतं धर्मं यस्य वक्ता न विद्यते ।\nदिव्यप्रभावः सुमहानृषिरेव मतोऽसि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"You speak true and kind dharma, of which no speaker is found; I consider you a very great seer of divine power."}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"ब्राह्मणा वै महाभागाः पितरोऽग्रभुजः सदा ।\nतेषां सर्वात्मना कार्यं प्रियं लोके मनीषिणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins are of great fortune, the ancestors who always eat first. A wise man in the world should do what pleases them in every way."}},{"n":14,"text":"यत्तेषां च प्रियं तत्ते वक्ष्यामि द्विजसत्तम ।\nनमस्कृत्वा ब्राह्मणेभ्यो ब्राह्मीं विद्यां निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will tell you what pleases them, best of brahmins; bowing to the brahmins, learn from me the knowledge of Brahman."}},{"n":15,"text":"इदं विश्वं जगत्सर्वमजय्यं चापि सर्वशः ।\nमहाभूतात्मकं ब्रह्मन्नातः परतरं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this universe, the whole world, unconquerable in every way, is made of the great elements, brahmin; nothing is higher than this."}},{"n":16,"text":"महाभूतानि खं वायुरग्निरापस्तथा च भूः ।\nशब्दः स्पर्शश्च रूपं च रसो गन्धश्च तद्गुणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great elements are space, wind, fire, water and earth; their qualities are sound, touch, form, taste and smell."}},{"n":17,"text":"तेषामपि गुणाः सर्वे गुणवृत्तिः परस्परम् ।\nपूर्वपूर्वगुणाः सर्वे क्रमशो गुणिषु त्रिषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their qualities all depend on one another; the qualities of each earlier one are found in order in the following three."}},{"n":18,"text":"षष्ठस्तु चेतना नाम मन इत्यभिधीयते ।\nसप्तमी तु भवेद्बुद्धिरहंकारस्ततः परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sixth is consciousness, called mind; the seventh is intellect, and beyond that is ego."}},{"n":19,"text":"इन्द्रियाणि च पञ्चैव रजः सत्त्वं तमस्तथा ।\nइत्येष सप्तदशको राशिरव्यक्तसंज्ञकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are five senses, and also passion, goodness and darkness. This heap of seventeen is called the unmanifest."}},{"n":20,"text":"सर्वैरिहेन्द्रियार्थैस्तु व्यक्ताव्यक्तैः सुसंवृतः ।\nचतुर्विंशक इत्येष व्यक्ताव्यक्तमयो गुणः ।\nएतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं किं भूयो श्रोतुमिच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this is well covered by all the objects of the senses, manifest and unmanifest. This quality, made of the manifest and unmanifest, makes twenty-four. I have told you all this; what more do you wish to hear?"}}]}]}